# Repository Structure

## Purpose

Documents the **current canonical** flat layout. Do not refactor toward a staged migration tree without an explicit task.

## Current canonical layout

Production code uses **flat domain packages**, not layered ceremony subtrees.

| Package | Role |
| :--- | :--- |
| `internal/controlplane/` | Admin API, outbox workers, billing, fraud admin, reports (~500 files, one package) |
| `internal/ingestion/` | Hot path: gnet, filters, stream, track, registry glue |
| `internal/control/` | Monolith runner for `cmd/control` |
| `internal/fraud/` | ML scoring (cold); admin fraud handlers stay in controlplane |
| `internal/domain/` | Shared hot-path types, sharding, budget invariants |
| `internal/<svc>/` | Side domains: `payment/`, `ledger/`, `notify/`, `identity/`, `edge/`, `rtb/`, `openrtb/` |

Module: `ad-event-processor`. `cmd/<binary>/main.go` wires config only - no business logic in `main`.

## Allowed vs banned subtrees

| Allowed subdirs | Banned ceremony |
| :--- | :--- |
| `db/`, `queries/`, `migrations/`, `pb/` | `dto/`, `usecase/`, `providers/`, `repositories/` |
| `controlplane/authz/`, `controlplane/outboxpb/` | Generic `services/` subtrees |

Root clutter: `core.mdc` Sources-only repository.

## cmd map

| Role | Binaries |
| :--- | :--- |
| Hot path | `tracker`, `campaign-shard` |
| Cold ingest | `processor`, `broker`, log pipeline |
| Control plane | `control`, `admin`, `operator`, `postback-sender`, `dlq` |
| Fraud / ML | `fraud-scorer`, `ivt-detector`, `ml-validate`, `ml-replay` |
| Edge | `edge-xdp`, `edge-bpf-sync`, `region-proxy` |
| Licensing / vendor | `license-issue`, `trial-registry`, `vendor-trial-bot` |

## Dependency arrows

```
cmd -> internal/control | cmd/*/main
ingest hot path must NOT import controlplane admin or internal/fraud scoring
pkg/* must NOT import internal/*
```

Tracker (`internal/ingestion`) must not import `internal/controlplane` admin handlers or `internal/fraud` scoring. `pkg/*` is shared utilities only - no `internal/*` imports.

## Future target (do not implement opportunistically)

Planned split map (not current):

- `controlplane` -> `campaign/`, `billing/`, `fraud/admin/`, ...
- `ingestion` -> `ingest/`, `filter/`, `stream/`, `track/`

Package cap when splitting: ~40 files or ~8k LOC per package; one domain per package; each domain gets `doc.go` with invariants.

